<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pagaruyung</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Istano Basa Pagaruyung</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pagaruyung is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanah-datar">Tanah Datar</a> regency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-sumatra">West Sumatra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, the seat of the Minangkabau royal house from the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adityawarman">Adityawarman</a> in the 14th century. The royal family was largely killed during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padri-war">Padri War</a> around 1815. A large replica of the royal palace, the Istano Basa, stands there today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pagaruyung.jpg" alt="Pagaruyung" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RahmatdenasMuffin Wizard This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Minang.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
